														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3712084">
									

<p>It feels like there are so many angles you could take this idea (eg what happens if a subject sees its rabbit breeding? does each affected subject pick a different rabbit and if not, then what? what if their pet dog kills the rabbit? what if the happy couple leaves Chattanooga valley? what if the rabbit has baby rabbits? not all marriages are happy - how does that work with rabbits?) and the choice to go with &quot;it's deeper than amnestics&quot; seems like a really unproductive one. It doesn't really lead anywhere, and I think that is evidenced by the third log which takes a very long time to make a carrot joke.</p>
<p>There's also the implication that amnestics don't work effectively when it comes to the wiping of any long-term partner, which slightly undermines how they're treated elsewhere. And why do the Containment Procedures make no attempt to (a) contain the rabbit population; or (b) restrict access / habitation in the area of effect?</p>

							</div>

								
					
